statement:
Let $Y$ be a scheme with small pro-etale site $Y_{\mathrm{proet}}$ [def-weil-pbc-proetale-site], let $\mathcal R$ be a sheaf of commutative rings on $Y_{\mathrm{proet}}$, and let $(F_n,t_n:F_{n+1}\to F_n)_{n\geq1}$ be an inverse system of sheaves of $\mathcal R$-modules [def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category] in which every $t_n$ is surjective (an epimorphism of sheaves). Let $\varprojlim_nF_n$ be its inverse limit [def-pur-sheaf-inverse-limit], with projections $p_n$, and let $D(Y_{\mathrm{proet}},\mathcal R)$ be the derived category of sheaves of $\mathcal R$-modules [def-weil-abstract-derived-category], every sheaf viewed as a complex in degree $0$. Then:

1. the map $1-s:\prod_nF_n\to\prod_nF_n$, $(x_n)_n\mapsto(x_n-t_n(x_{n+1}))_n$, is surjective, and its kernel is $\varprojlim_nF_n$ (via $(p_n)_n$), so $0\to\varprojlim_nF_n\to\prod_nF_n\xrightarrow{1-s}\prod_nF_n\to0$ is a short exact sequence of sheaves of $\mathcal R$-modules;
2. the sheaf $\prod_nF_n$ in degree $0$, with its projections, is a product of the $F_n$ in $D(Y_{\mathrm{proet}},\mathcal R)$, and the distinguished triangle $\varprojlim_nF_n\to\prod_nF_n\xrightarrow{1-s}\prod_nF_n\to(\varprojlim_nF_n)[1]$ of this short exact sequence is a Roos triangle, so that $\varprojlim_nF_n$ in degree $0$ is a derived limit $R\varprojlim_nF_n$ of the system in $D(Y_{\mathrm{proet}},\mathcal R)$ [def-weil-derived-limit];
3. for every sheaf $G$ of $\mathcal R$-modules and every family of morphisms $g_n:G\to F_n$ with $t_n g_{n+1}=g_n$, there is exactly one morphism $G\to R\varprojlim_nF_n=\varprojlim_nF_n$ in $D(Y_{\mathrm{proet}},\mathcal R)$ whose composite with $\varprojlim_nF_n\to\prod_nF_n$ is $(g_n)_n$, namely the morphism of sheaves induced by the universal property of the limit (two such morphisms differ by a morphism $G\to(\prod_nF_n)[-1]$, and there is none but $0$ between sheaves placed in degrees $0$ and $1$).
